module engine where

-- field-key — the keys of the field-identity kernel.
--
-- A field slot is keyed by a FieldKey: a named field by a reference to its
-- `Field` entity, a positional field by its ordinal. SetExpr's `SetCtorField`
-- and `SetArrowParam` and the compiler IR use these keys, so
-- `modules/set-expr-entities.ts` publishes both types in the system and seed
-- registries beside SetExpr. The rest of the kernel is field-identity.fenel.
--
-- `FieldRef { handle }` is the `$`-free kernel view of a reference to a `Field`
-- (design/field-identity.md); the B3 boundary maps it to the stored
-- `{$ref: handle}`. Making the published type describe the stored form is the
-- general typed-reference follow-up.

FieldRef = FieldRef handle: String

FieldKey =
  NamedField ref: FieldRef
  | PositionalField index: Nat
